{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user wants me to implement a `solve(case)` function for HDBSCAN mutual reachability MST computation, and return it as a JSON object with key \"implementation\". Let me analyze the task:\n\n1. For each pair of nodes, compute mutual reachability = max(core_distance[left], core_distance[right], distance)\n2. Canonicalize undirected endpoints (sort them)\n3. Sort edges by reachability, then endpoint IDs\n4. Run Kruskal's algorithm with union-find until n-1 edges selected\n5. Return selected edges + total weight\n6. Reject disconnected inputs\n\nThe response format must be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source.\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case.get(\"nodes\")\n    core_distance = case.get(\"core_distance\")\n    distances = case.get(\"distances\")\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    if nodes is None or core_distance is None or distances is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required fields\")\n    \n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"nodes must be a non-empty list\")\n    \n    for node in nodes:\n        if node not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Missing core_distance for node {node}\")\n    \n    # Compute mutual reachability for each pair\n    edges = []\n    for entry in distances:\n        u, v, dist = entry[0], entry[1], entry[2]\n        # Canonicalize endpoints\n        if u \u003e v:\n            u, v = v, u\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], dist)\n        edges.append((mr, u, v))\n    \n    # Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs\n    edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\n    \n    # Kruskal's MST with union-find\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    mst_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n    \n    for mr, u, v in edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mr])\n            total_weight += mr\n            if len(mst_edges) == len(nodes) - 1:\n                break\n    \n    # Check if MST spans all nodes\n    if len(mst_edges) != len(nodes) - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Graph is disconnected\")\n    \n    return {\n        \"mst_edges\": mst_edges,\n        \"total_weight\": total_weight\n    }\n```\n\nNow I need to format this as a JSON object. Let me be careful about the JSON encoding - newlines become \\n, backslashes become \\\\, quotes become \\\".\n\nLet me construct the final JSON response properly.\n\nThe note says the first non-whitespace character must be { and last must be }. No markdown. Just raw JSON.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case.get(\\\"nodes\\\")\\n    core_distance = case.get(\\\"core_distance\\\")\\n    distances = case.get(\\\"distances\\\")\\n\\n    if nodes is None or core_distance is None or distances is None:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required fields: nodes, core_distance, distances\\\")\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or len(nodes) == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"nodes must be a non-empty list\\\")\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if node not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing core_distance for node {node!r}\\\")\\n\\n    # Build mutual-reachability edges\\n    mr_edges = []\\n    for entry in distances:\\n        if len(entry) != 3:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Distance entry must have 3 elements: {entry!r}\\\")\\n        a, b, dist = entry[0], entry[1], float(entry[2])\\n        if a not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Unknown node in distances: {a!r}\\\")\\n        if b not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Unknown node in distances: {b!r}\\\")\\n        # Canonicalize undirected endpoints\\n        u, v = (a, b) if a \u003c= b else (b, a)\\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], dist)\\n        mr_edges.append((mr, u, v))\\n\\n    # Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs (deterministic tie-breaking)\\n    mr_edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\\n\\n    # Kruskal's MST with path-compressed union-find\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n\\n    def find(x):\\n        root = x\\n        while parent[root] != root:\\n            root = parent[root]\\n        # Path compression\\n        while parent[x] != root:\\n            parent[x], x = root, parent[x]\\n        return root\\n\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\\n        parent[ry] = rx\\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n\\n    mst_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n\\n    for mr, u, v in mr_edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            mst_edges.append([u, v, mr])\\n            total_weight += mr\\n            if len(mst_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n\\n    if len(mst_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Input graph is disconnected; cannot form a spanning tree\\\")\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"mst_edges\\\": mst_edges,\\n        \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01lJf0iJnuIPLJyRERiMVYia","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":1910,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":18,"output_tokens":1598,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":814},"service_tier":"standard"}}